# Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace @your-org/release-reviewers with
# the people or team who approve releases. With "Require review from Code
# Owners" turned on, a pull request that changes any of these paths cannot
# merge without their approval. See docs/ci.md in the skill.
#
# Change the test and manifest paths below to match your repository. Every
# command recorded in the audit runs code from these paths, so a weakened test
# or a swapped dependency would otherwise change the result without review.

# The workflow that runs the gate, and this file.
/.github/workflows/ @your-org/release-reviewers
/.github/CODEOWNERS @your-org/release-reviewers

# The release gate and the rest of the skill.
/.agents/skills/application-guardian/ @your-org/release-reviewers

# The audit result. Accepted risks, approvers, and the commands CI re-runs live here.
/docs/audits/audit-result.json @your-org/release-reviewers

# The tests that prove the mandatory checks, and their configuration.
/tests/ @your-org/release-reviewers
/pytest.ini @your-org/release-reviewers
/pyproject.toml @your-org/release-reviewers
/jest.config.* @your-org/release-reviewers
/vitest.config.* @your-org/release-reviewers
/playwright.config.* @your-org/release-reviewers

# Dependency manifests and lockfiles, which decide what the test runners load.
/package.json @your-org/release-reviewers
/package-lock.json @your-org/release-reviewers
/pnpm-lock.yaml @your-org/release-reviewers
/yarn.lock @your-org/release-reviewers
/requirements*.txt @your-org/release-reviewers
/poetry.lock @your-org/release-reviewers
/uv.lock @your-org/release-reviewers
